  "task": {
    "objective": "Runners recover cipher and carry it to exact exit tile; wardens seek both runners restrained first. Extraction pays each runner +1 and each warden -1; both-captured reverses rewards. Unresolved horizon pays zero.",
    "natural_termination": "Extraction or both runners captured after rescue resolution ends naturally. Otherwise horizon 96, with natural priority. Terminal calls absorb preserving state and returning zero reward.",
    "interaction": "Opposed gate control, shared batteries, cipher dropping on tag, adjacent partner rescue, disclosed sensing relays, cloaks and scanners alter route feasibility, information and future interception.",
    "observation_access": "Public static map, exit, active devices/flares, clock and extraction status. Manhattan sensors through walls: courier radius 2, others 3. Friendly flares relay radius-three agent sensing and expose emitter to opponents. Cloaks hide nearby runners beyond adjacency; live flare or scanner overrides. Wardens share scanner radius 4. Carried cipher follows carrier visibility; grounded cipher, gates and caches use direct local range. Own-team energy only. Scene events exclude private capture and remote gate changes."
